ClassInChowRing -- Gives the class of a hypersurface in the associated Chow ring of a product of projective spaces
******************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ClassInToricChowRing(A,f)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, the Chow ring of
        \PP^{n_1} x...x\PP^{n_1}
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element of the
        coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1} x...x\PP^{n_1}
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the class of V(f),
        [V(f)] in the Chow ring of \PP^{n_1} x...x\PP^{n_1}

Description
===========

This method finds the class [V(f)] of the hypersurface V(f) where f is a
polynomial in the graded coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1} x...x\PP^{n_1}. The class
[V(f)] is an element of the Chow ring of  \PP^{n_1} x...x\PP^{n_1}. Consider
\PP^3x\PP^4x\PP^1

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R=MultiProjCoordRing({3,4,1})|
|                                  |
|o1 = R                            |
|                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing               |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : A=ChowRing(R)                |
|                                  |
|o2 = A                            |
|                                  |
|o2 : QuotientRing                 |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : f=random({1,1,1},R);         |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : ClassInChowRing(A,f)         |
|                                  |
|o4 = h  + h  + h                  |
|      1    2    3                 |
|                                  |
|o4 : A                            |
+----------------------------------+

Ways to use ClassInChowRing:
============================

  * "ClassInChowRing(QuotientRing,RingElement)"

