EulerAffine -- The Euler Characteristic of an affine variety.
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        EulerAffine I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in a polynomial ring
        over a field defining an affine variety.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Euler
        characteristic

Description
===========

This command computes the Euler characteristic of a complex affine variety.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : kk=ZZ/32749;                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=kk[x_1..x_3]                                    |
|                                                       |
|o2 = R                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I=ideal(x_1^2+x_2^2+x_3^2-1)                      |
|                                                       |
|            2    2    2                                |
|o3 = ideal(x  + x  + x  - 1)                           |
|            1    2    3                                |
|                                                       |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : time EulerAffine I                                |
| -- used 0.0663021s (cpu); 0.0660964s (thread); 0s (gc)|
|                                                       |
|o4 = 2                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

Observe that the algorithm is a probabilistic algorithm and may give a wrong
answer with a small but nonzero probability. Read more under *note
probabilistic algorithm: probabilistic algorithm,.

Ways to use EulerAffine:
========================

